      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The idea sounds good, but I can see many ways it can be abused. People already block, kick, mute, etc, for no (or bad) reasons a lot of the time. I remember myself getting kicked out of an instance once for simply asking politely the instance owner if he could turn off or down the music he was playing through his mic. I know I could have muted him, but I chose to first try and ask politely, and got hit with a kick instead. The point is people like that would unjustly lower people's rep. New trolls could also arise that block and mute people just to lower their rep. This could also be abused the other way around, if a group of trolls/crashers decided to get together and give plus rep to one person in the group, then they can use that high rep to gain peoples trust (or bypass the low rep automatic block), then go and do whatever damage they feel like. This would be an interesting feature, but there would have to be a lot of things put into place that protects the system from being abused. It might work, but it could also end up being more effort than it's worth.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
